:: Widgets MMA Gym [widget]
<<widget "mmaGymIntro">>
	<<set $mmaGymIntroExit to _args[0]>><<set $mmagymintro to 1>>
	You pay the receptionist, who barely glances at you before nodding toward the gym floor. The smell of sweat and rubber mats hits you as you step inside. Heavy bags hang from the ceiling, a ring stands in the centre, and fighters are working through their drills. Near the entrance, a row of new treadmills and a glass-fronted VIP lounge look much more expensive than the rest of the gym.
	<br><br>
	It's easy to pick out the coach. <<He>> has short dark brown hair in a slightly messy undercut, damp with sweat, above a weathered but sharp face. <<His>> body is lean and scarred from years of fighting. <<He>> wears simple gear: hand wraps, a sleeveless hoodie and fight shorts.
	<br><br>

	<<if $NPCList[0].breastsize gte 5>>
		Despite <<his>> hardened appearance, <<his>> generous breasts are bound tight, keeping them streamlined for movement.
	<<elseif $NPCList[0].breastsize gte 3>>
		<<His>> breasts are bound close to <<his>> torso, keeping them compact for training.
	<<elseif $NPCList[0].breastsize gte 1>>
		<<His>> small breasts are pressed flat against <<his>> chest, making them appear even leaner.
	<<else>>
		<<His>> flat chest gives <<him>> a wiry, no-nonsense look.
	<</if>>
	<<if $NPCList[0].penissize gt 1>>
		You catch a brief glimpse of a bulge pressing against <<his>> shorts, but <<his>> stance makes it clear <<he>> doesn't care if you notice.
	<</if>>

	<br><br>
	When the door swings shut behind you, the coach turns and looks you up and down with sharp black eyes. "New blood? Hope you're not here for some light cardio. I'm Riley. Who are you?"
	<br><br>

